human_thriving v8 is not published to HuggingFace Hub.

WHAT THIS FILE IS FOR. `scripts/deployment/verify_filter_package.py --check-hub` cannot
otherwise tell "we deliberately did not publish this" from "the hub check is broken": with
no `inference_hub.py` it short-circuits at "skip: inference_hub.py not present" and then
fails with "cannot check — no repo_id extracted". That failure blocked a commit on
2026-09-04 and was the correct behaviour — absence and declaration read identically without
this file. NexusMind's `filter_loader` sets `hub_class = None` from the same absence.

⛔ THE DECISION IS NO LONGER OPEN — owner ruled 2026-09-06: PUBLISH, as an
off-machine backup. It has not happened yet, so this file is still true.

⛔ AND `inference_hub.py` MUST NOT LAND BEFORE THE REPO EXISTS. `verify_filter_package.py`
refuses the pair outright — *"NO_HUB sentinel present but inference_hub.py also exists —
ambiguous deploy state"* — and it blocked a commit for exactly that on 2026-09-06. The
module is written and verified (repo id resolves, 7/7 with this file removed); it is held
out of the tree until the transfer runs. THE ORDER IS: publish, verify, then commit
`inference_hub.py` and DELETE this file in one commit. Never the other way round — #44's
whole lesson is that a claim in a message does not make the transfer happen.

⚠️ The reason to publish got STRONGER on 2026-09-06. The owner rejected recording a
provenance exception for the un-reproducible checkpoint and had it retrained under a
commit on `main`, so the tree that builds the adapter is now pinned — but the 82 MB
artifact itself is still held by exactly one machine, and a pinned recipe is not a
backup of the thing it produced.

⚠️ THE TEXT BELOW RECORDS THE STATE BEFORE THAT RULING.
`docs/HUMAN_THRIVING_V8_PLAN.md` §3c calls a Hub repo for v8 **optional**. So this file
says "not published today", not "never publish".

⭐ AND v8's REASON IS NOT v7's — read this before copying the precedent.
`filters/uplifting/v7/NO_HUB` gives a substantive reason: v7 was rsync'd from gpu-server
without `training_metadata.json` / `training_history.json`, so building a Hub model card
would have meant reconstructing metrics from a README narrative — fabricating numbers the
card would then present as ground truth.

**That reason does not apply to v8.** v8 ships both files, committed
(`filters/human_thriving/v8/training_{metadata,history}.json`, EXP-015), plus
`calibration_report.md` and a full evidence directory. A Hub model card for v8 could be
built from measured artifacts. The route is genuinely open; it simply has not been taken.

WHAT WOULD MAKE PUBLISHING WORTH IT: an off-machine backup of the weights. Today the LoRA
adapter exists in exactly two places — `b650-gpu:~/llm-distillery/filters/human_thriving/v8/model/`
and (after Phase F) NexusMind. Neither is a backup of the other in any meaningful sense.
Against that: a Hub repo is another surface to keep in sync, and #48 requires the repo be
named `human-thriving-filter-v8` or `verify_filter_package.py` fails on the mismatch.

IF THIS IS REVISITED: delete this file, run
`scripts/deployment/upload_to_huggingface.py --filter filters/human_thriving/v8
--repo-name jeergrvgreg/human-thriving-filter-v8 --token $HF_TOKEN --private`, and
⛔ do NOT run `resave_adapter.py` first — it rewrites the PEFT keys into the new format and
breaks `PeftModel.from_pretrained()` (CLAUDE.md Hard Constraints).

